 "note_GAPS6": "2 Oct 2026 (GAPS6-pro3055-clinton-1779): crops of Image 1205 cut by tools/iiif_lines.py --image with --centres set by eye (the autocorrelation pitch misread the narrow columns) from a 5512-px native copy held in the session scratchpad; the worker inverted that copy before cropping believing the frame a negative, so every crop here is polarity-inverted (white ink on grey) relative to the served frame img1205_w1600.jpg -- the passes read them as such; regenerate un-inverted by refetching full/max and re-running the recorded commands without the inversion. Hand crops: p123_lac_label.jpg = native box (4750,1450,5190,2755) rotated -90; p123_binding_label.jpg = native box (4495,3390,5040,3535). Region recipe (native px, x,y,w,h): margin 2100,620,600,980 centres 160,406,468,548,627,722,812,903; clearcol 3600,2860,460,940 centres 52,146,240,327,418,509,596,679,766,838; head 2100,620,1950,240 (auto); foot 2860,3660,1200,140 centres 40,100; p122_head 220,760,1870,400 centres 56,219,328; p122_close 220,2050,1870,800 centres 80,170,260,360,640,730; p122_* crops re-encoded at 0.8 scale quality 55 and the LAC label at quality 65 to keep the folder under 30 MiB."
